      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for arranging and paying for both the freight and insurance to deliver the goods to the named port of destination. However, the risk of loss or damage to the electronic shipment transfers to you once the goods are loaded onto the vessel at the port of export, meaning any incidents during ocean transit are your liability. You should also ensure your contract explicitly clarifies that while you pay costs, you retain control of the shipment until delivery, protecting yourself from unexpected freight price hikes or delays.",
