    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thx. ok so if the risk transfers at the port of export, what kind of insurance coverage should we be looking for specifically? i want to make sure we're covered if something goes wrong mid-transit.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since risk transfers to you at the port of export, you must purchase your own insurance immediately upon handing over the goods to the carrier to protect against transit losses. Under CIF, the seller typically provides minimum coverage (often \"FPA\" or minimal physical damage), which may not be sufficient for high-value electronics requiring comprehensive protection against total loss or theft. You should negotiate the contract to include specific language requiring the seller to provide a certificate for Institute Cargo Clauses A, which offers broad all-risk coverage matching your shipment's value.",
