    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. i'll check on those clauses. one more thing, can u give me a quick list of the main differences between CIF and CIP? just want to be sure i'm not mixing them up before i send this to the legal team.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary difference lies in the mode of transport: CIF is strictly for sea waterways, while CIP covers all other modes including air, rail, and road. Consequently, if your electronics shipment involves trucking to the port or an airport, using CIF could render the contract void or misaligned with CIP. Another key distinction is insurance; CIP requires the seller to provide comprehensive \"all-risk\" insurance coverage, whereas CIF often defaults to minimum liability clauses unless specified otherwise. You should verify the intended destination port or final delivery point to ensure the chosen term matches your logistics plan.",
